        "readme": "<p>This module demonstrates how Serenity/JS integrates with Playwright Test&#39;s component testing mode to test individual UI components in isolation.</p>\n<h2>Why component testing?</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Test components in isolation without running the full application</li>\n<li>Faster feedback loop than end-to-end tests</li>\n<li>Verify component behaviour, accessibility, and visual rendering</li>\n<li>Complements end-to-end tests by covering component-level edge cases</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Why Serenity/JS?</h2>\n<p>Serenity/JS provides:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Screenplay Pattern</strong> – interact with mounted components using the same Tasks, Interactions, and Questions used in full-page tests</li>\n<li><strong>Rich reporting</strong> – activity trees show component interactions with the same detail as end-to-end tests</li>\n<li><strong>Consistent API</strong> – <code>@serenity-js/web</code> interactions work identically in component and full-page testing modes</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Features demonstrated</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Mounting components within Playwright Test&#39;s component testing harness</li>\n<li>Serenity/JS fixtures and actor integration in component test mode</li>\n<li>Web interactions (Click, Enter, assertions) against isolated components</li>\n</ul>\n"
